  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the amount of money that Noah received:\n\n$$\n$1215⟶$1200\n$$\n\nThe ratio of Emma's earnings to Noah's earnings is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents Emma's earnings  and the denominator represents Noah's earnings.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $1200$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $400$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 400}{3\\times 400}=\\frac{2800}{1200}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Emma received approximately $$2800.$",
